.TH AGENT-HOOK-PERMISSION-REQUEST 1 "2026-11-18" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-permission-request \- answer agent permission prompts when opted in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-permission-request
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-permission-request
handles the
.B PermissionRequest
event. It is opt-in as a whole: unless
.B AGENTGUARD_PERMISSION_REQUEST_ALLOW
is enabled it prints empty JSON and exits before reading its input, loading
extensions, writing an audit record, or creating session state.
.PP
When enabled, it reads the payload, sources its extensions, and answers with
an allow decision if one of them called
.BR _hook_allow_permission ;
otherwise the response is empty JSON and the agent prompts as usual. The base
hook decides nothing itself; the requests a runtime may answer are its
extension's rule, such as
.BR agent-hook-permission-request-claude (1).
When another PermissionRequest hook denies the same request, the deny wins.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_PERMISSION_REQUEST_ALLOW
Set to
.B 1
to let the hook and its extensions answer permission requests. Read from the
hook/launcher environment, including a Claude Code settings-file
.B env
block; an
.B export
in an agent tool shell cannot reach hook processes, but an agent session it
starts inherits the value.
.SH EXTENSIONS
AgentGuard sources
.I agent-hook-permission-request-<agent>
and
.I agent-hook-permission-request-work
only while the knob is enabled. An extension calls
.B _hook_allow_permission
to answer allow, or
.B _hook_block
to withdraw an allow; a block never turns the answer into a deny.
.SH TELEMETRY
While enabled, each run writes one hook record whose
.B decision
field is
.B allow
when it answered; see
.BR agentguard-telemetry (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Always, unless the install is broken (see 2), whether or not the hook
answered.
.TP
.B 2
A broken install: the hook cannot find its path or load the AgentGuard
helpers. Claude ignores exit status 2 on this event and shows the prompt as
usual; only a printed decision counts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-permission-request-claude (1),
.BR agent-hook-telemetry (1),
.BR agentguard-telemetry (1)
